-- Q958: Entity Tax Compliance: NOLs and Consolidated Returns [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treas. Reg. Section 1.1502-21(b)(2), when a member departs a consolidated group, it takes its apportioned share of the CNOL based on the member''s contribution to the loss. Member A contributed $200,000 of the $300,000 CNOL, so it takes $200,000 upon departure. The remaining $100,000 stays with the continuing group.
Wrong (A): $300,000 is the total CNOL for the entire group, not the departing member''s share. Departure apportionment is proportional, not total.
Wrong (C): $100,000 is the portion attributable to Member B, not Member A. Each member takes only the loss it contributed.
Wrong (D): A departing member does not forfeit its CNOL share. The regulations specifically provide for proportional allocation upon departure.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 958;

