  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1297(a)(1), a foreign corporation is classified as a PFIC if 75% or more of its gross income consists of passive income (the income test). Alternatively, under Section 1297(a)(2), the asset test classifies a corporation as a PFIC if 50% or more of assets produce passive income. The 75% income test is the primary threshold.
Wrong (A): The 50% threshold applies to the asset test under Section 1297(a)(2), not the income test. The income test requires 75%.
Wrong (B): 60% is not a threshold under either the PFIC income test or the asset test.
