  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 951A(b), net GILTI equals total tested income minus the net deemed tangible income return (DTIR). DTIR is 10% of aggregate QBAI: 10% x $20,000,000 = $2,000,000. Net GILTI = $5,000,000 - $2,000,000 = $3,000,000. A domestic C corporation may then claim a 50% Section 250 deduction on this amount.
Wrong (A): $5,000,000 is the gross tested income before subtracting the DTIR. It ignores the QBAI offset entirely.
Wrong (C): $2,000,000 is the DTIR itself, not the net GILTI inclusion. It confuses the offset amount with the result.
Wrong (D): $0 would require QBAI of at least $50,000,000 to fully shelter the tested income. The $20,000,000 QBAI is insufficient to eliminate the inclusion.$EXPL$
